Module 2.3 — EDA with Applied Statistics

If by Module 2.3 you mean the third part of Module 2, it mainly covers Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) and Statistics.

1. Introduction to EDA

EDA (Exploratory Data Analysis) is the process of examining and understanding a dataset before applying Machine Learning or statistical models.

Main objectives

Understand the data

Find missing values

Detect outliers

Identify patterns and trends

Understand relationships between variables

Prepare data for further analysis


Example

Suppose we have student data:

Name	Age	Marks

Rahul	20	75
Sneha	21	90
Amit	20	65


Using EDA, we can find:

Average marks

Highest marks

Lowest marks

Distribution of marks

Relationship between age and marks



---

2. EDA vs Python Programming

Python Programming	EDA

General-purpose programming	Data analysis
Focuses on writing logic	Focuses on finding insights
Uses variables, loops, functions	Uses statistics and visualization
Can build applications	Helps understand datasets
Example: calculator program	Example: sales analysis


Simple example:

Python programming:

marks = [70, 80, 90]
print(sum(marks))

EDA:

import numpy as np

marks = np.array([70, 80, 90])

print("Mean:", np.mean(marks))
print("Maximum:", np.max(marks))
print("Minimum:", np.min(marks))


